# Trivy config scan (.github/workflows/security.yml's iac-scan job) findings
# accepted as documented risk, not silently suppressed - each one is also
# recorded in docs/security.md's "Not yet built" section or an existing ADR.
# Everything Trivy found that had no real functional/cost tradeoff was fixed
# instead of ignored - see the comments next to drop_invalid_header_fields,
# kms_master_key_id, map_public_ip_on_launch = false, and the RDS/Redis
# security groups' now-absent egress blocks in infrastructure/terraform.

# S3 bucket (bootstrap/main.tf) and SNS topic (modules/monitoring) are
# already encrypted at rest (SSE-S3 / the AWS-managed SNS key respectively) -
# these two findings specifically want a *customer-managed* KMS key instead,
# which costs $1/month per key with no benefit for a Terraform state bucket
# or an alarm-notification topic nobody has subscribed to yet.
AVD-AWS-0132
AVD-AWS-0136

# ECR image_tag_mutability is MUTABLE, matching the :latest-based push
# workflow docs/deployment.md documents today. Switching to IMMUTABLE is the
# right long-term answer (and a natural follow-up once Phase 13's real
# deployment work redesigns the tagging strategy around immutable SHA tags
# instead of a repeatedly-overwritten :latest), but doing it here would
# break that already-documented workflow without a live AWS account to
# verify the replacement against - the same "don't change what can't be
# tested against a real account" reasoning as the rest of Phase 12/13.
AVD-AWS-0031

# The ALB is deliberately internet-facing (it's how this app's own users
# reach it) and, per ADR-0013, HTTP-only until a real domain exists to issue
# a TLS certificate against - both already-documented decisions, not gaps.
AVD-AWS-0053
AVD-AWS-0054

# Remaining broad egress (ALB, frontend, backend, ai-service security
# groups - RDS/Redis were fixed to have no egress at all, since a database
# never initiates outbound traffic). Precisely scoping down egress for
# these four needs knowing exactly what each one calls outbound (AWS
# service endpoints for ECS/CloudWatch, the AI service's real LLM provider
# if one is ever configured, etc.) and verifying nothing breaks - not
# something to guess at without a live account to test against, given this
# project's deliberate decision not to spend money on one yet (see
# docs/deployment.md's Phase 13 section).
AVD-AWS-0104
